Honoured to receive the Albert Medal from
@theRSAorg! Science &amp; tech enable amazing opportunities, but the arts &amp; humanities will be crucial in shaping what sort of future we want to see as a society in the coming AGI era. Fun discussion w/
@FryRsquared covering many new topics:

Surprised with how good the comments on github gists are. A lot more helpful, insightful, constructive, a lot less AI... Is it the user community? The markdown format? The (lack of) incentives?

Suddenly feeling like I should gist more.
@github consider competing with X (?)

What can large-scale AI models bring to the growing complexity of particle physics?

@CERN  and Mistral join forces to explore this question.

The ambition: a single Large Physics Model, trained on billions of simulated collisions. https://t.co/nrdCfcBI3k

Entire industries will be built on open models.
Developers need the freedom to build them.

@JensenHuang on why keeping these models open and accessible matters. https://t.co/ib7QYMJdxU

An idea can only go so far without the computing power to test it.

@JensenHuang joined Wallenberg Investments’ Marcus Wallenberg, @Spotify’s @eldsjal, and Sferical AI’s Jenny Nordlöw to celebrate the launch of Sferical One, a shared AI supercomputer powered by NVIDIA.

More https://t.co/7jUtBW54rk

